From 648d9f780fef8d22c6e2469717d2407162eb3ddd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik <erik-131@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 04:05:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/41] NHL: GPU profile per render target and per resolve
 (dump and copy); test switches for half pixels, fast vertex math and dumping
 one sample

All off by default. Half pixels: main pass 5.2 -> 3.8 ms. Fast vertex math: 2-4 % fewer draw cycles at most. One-sample dump: 3.12 -> 2.66 ms in scenes with 4x shadow resolves, nothing elsewhere; validated by poisoning the skipped samples (clean) and keeping the wrong one (depth of field breaks).
